1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,520
Hello, welcome back to Daily English Talk.

2
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:04,440
Hi, everyone.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,080
We're so happy to see you.

4
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:07,200
I'm Emma.

5
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:08,280
And I'm Jack.

6
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:12,520
On this channel, we help you practice real, everyday English.

7
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:17,120
Please, if you like our video, don't forget to like and subscribe.

8
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,680
It helps us a lot.

9
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,480
Yes, please subscribe.

10
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,360
It makes Emma very happy.

11
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:27,520
Today, we are going to talk about a very common topic.

12
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:29,120
A very useful topic.

13
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:31,720
We are going to talk about our weekends.

14
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:35,620
That's right. Talking about your weekend. Let's begin.

15
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:38,320
So, Jack, how are you today?

16
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,920
I am great. Thank you. And you?

17
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:44,820
I'm pretty good. A little tired, but good.

18
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:48,320
Tired? Why are you tired? Did you have a busy weekend?

19
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:54,920
You know me too well. Yes, my weekend was very busy, but it was fun.

20
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:59,360
I want to hear about it, but first, let's talk to our friends.

21
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:00,360
Yes.

22
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,720
Hello, friends.

23
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:03,000
How are you?

24
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,600
How was your weekend?

25
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:06,420
Think about your answer.

26
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:07,860
Was it good?

27
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,380
Was it busy?

28
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:10,800
Was it relaxing?

29
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:14,760
We want to know, but first, you can listen to us.

30
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:16,060
Okay, Emma.

31
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:17,220
You first.

32
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:18,520
How was your weekend?

33
00:01:18,520 --> 00:01:20,780
My weekend was really nice.

34
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:22,400
It was eventful.

35
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:23,400
Eventful?

36
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:28,520
Eventful. That's a good word. It means many things happened.

37
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:34,120
Yes, many things happened. On Saturday morning, I woke up early.

38
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:39,640
Early? On a Saturday? Why? Saturday is for sleeping.

39
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:47,160
I know, I know, but I had plans. I met my friend, Sarah, for coffee.

40
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:49,640
Oh, nice. Where did you go?

41
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:53,800
We went to that new cafe downtown, the Coffee Corner.

42
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:55,680
I know that place.

43
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:56,480
Is it good?

44
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:58,320
It's excellent.

45
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:01,080
The coffee was delicious.

46
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:03,760
And I had a blueberry muffin.

47
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,760
It was so tasty.

48
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:09,260
I love muffins.

49
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:13,040
So you had coffee with Sarah for how long?

50
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:16,720
For about two hours, we talked a lot.

51
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:22,720
We talked about our jobs, our families, and we made plans for next weekend.

52
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:26,720
Sounds like a perfect Saturday morning. What did you do after that?

53
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:30,720
After that, I went to the supermarket. I needed food for the week.

54
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:34,720
Ah, grocery shopping. Not so fun.

55
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:42,720
It's okay. I don't mind it. I bought milk, bread, fruit, and some chicken for dinner.

56
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:50,020
dinner. So for lunch, what did you have for lunch on Saturday? For lunch, I was

57
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:56,140
still at the supermarket, so I just had a small sandwich at home. A quick lunch. I

58
00:02:56,140 --> 00:03:03,540
see. And the afternoon, tell me about the afternoon. In the afternoon, I went for a

59
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:09,740
walk in the park. The weather was beautiful, sunny and warm. Oh, that's

60
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:17,340
lovely. Was the park busy? Yes, it was very busy. Many families were there. Children were playing.

61
00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:24,860
It was very lively. Did you walk alone? Yes, I walked alone. I listened to music. It was very

62
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:33,980
relaxing. Nice. So a busy morning and a relaxing afternoon. What about the evening? Evening was

63
00:03:33,980 --> 00:03:41,900
the best part. I went to the cinema. Oh, what movie did you see? I saw the new comedy movie,

64
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:49,580
The Funny Cat. Have you heard of it? Yes, I want to see it. Was it good? It was hilarious.

65
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:57,340
I laughed so much. My face hurt from laughing. That's a good sign. Who did you go with?

66
00:03:57,340 --> 00:04:02,780
I went with my brother, Tom. He also thought the movie was very funny. And after the

67
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:09,580
movie? After the movie, we were hungry, so we went to a pizza restaurant. My favorite. What kind of

68
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:19,900
pizza? We had a large pizza with mushrooms and olives. It was delicious. Wow, Emma. Your Saturday

69
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:30,860
was full. Coffee, shopping, walk, movie, pizza. No wonder you're tired. Yes, but it was a good tired.

70
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:34,540
Now, your turn, Jack. How was your weekend?

71
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:37,740
My weekend was different.

72
00:04:37,740 --> 00:04:41,340
Different? What does that mean? Was it good?

73
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:46,700
It was good, but very, very quiet. Very relaxing.

74
00:04:47,420 --> 00:04:48,460
Tell me about it.

75
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:53,020
Okay. On Saturday, I woke up very late.

76
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:56,140
Of course you did.

77
00:04:56,140 --> 00:04:59,020
It was 11 o'clock. It was wonderful.

78
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:03,220
11 o'clock? That is very late.

79
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:06,980
I know. I was very tired from last week. I needed rest.

80
00:05:06,980 --> 00:05:10,420
So you woke up at 11. Then what?

81
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:14,900
Then I made a big breakfast. Well, it was breakfast and lunch together.

82
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,020
Brunch!

83
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:20,180
Yes, brunch. I made eggs, toast, and I had some orange juice.

84
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:21,300
That sounds nice.

85
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:24,820
It was. Then I sat on my sofa and I read a book.

86
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:28,420
You read a book? I'm surprised. What book?

87
00:05:28,420 --> 00:05:32,580
It's a mystery novel. It's very interesting. I read for about two hours.

88
00:05:32,580 --> 00:05:34,420
That sounds so peaceful.

89
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:39,620
It was. In the afternoon, I did some cleaning.

90
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:44,340
You cleaning? Now I am very surprised.

91
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:49,460
Hey, I can clean. I cleaned my kitchen and I washed some clothes.

92
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:53,620
Good for you. So, your apartment is nice and clean now.

93
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:58,820
Yes, for one or two days at least. Then in the evening I ordered food.

94
00:05:58,820 --> 00:05:59,780
From where?

95
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:04,020
From the Thai restaurant near my house. I had green curry. It's my favorite.

96
00:06:04,020 --> 00:06:07,460
Yummy. And then did you watch TV?

97
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:12,740
Yes, I watched a football game on TV. My team played. It was an exciting game.

98
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:14,260
Did your team win?

99
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:16,820
Yes, they did. 2-1. It was a great game.

100
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:24,340
So, your Saturday was sleep, eat, read, clean, eat, watch TV.

101
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:28,900
Exactly. It was perfect. I didn't leave my apartment all day.

102
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:34,100
That is very different from my day. And what about Sunday? Was Sunday the same?

103
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:38,180
Sunday was a little different. In the morning, I went to my parents' house.

104
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:40,500
Oh, that's nice. How are they?

105
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:43,700
They are great. My mom cooked a big lunch for us.

106
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:44,820
What did she make?

107
00:06:44,820 --> 00:06:51,700
she made roast chicken with potatoes and vegetables. It was so good. My mom is the best cook.

108
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:55,220
That sounds delicious. I'm a little jealous.

109
00:06:55,220 --> 00:07:00,820
You should be. After lunch, we drank tea and talked for a long time.

110
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:01,940
What did you talk about?

111
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:07,700
We talked about many things. My job, their garden, my sister. It was nice.

112
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:10,900
Family time is the best. What time did you go home?

113
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:15,700
I went home at about 5 p.m. Then I called my friend on the phone.

114
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:16,420
Which friend?

115
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:20,340
My friend David. We talked for an hour. He told me about his new job.

116
00:07:20,340 --> 00:07:21,860
And after the call?

117
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:27,700
After the call, I prepared for the week. I chose my clothes for work. I made a list of things to do.

118
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:30,580
You are so organized. I'm impressed.

119
00:07:30,580 --> 00:07:35,780
Thank you. Then I watched a documentary about animals and I went to bed early.

120
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:39,540
So, your weekend was very quiet and relaxing.

121
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:43,780
Yes, it was. I feel very rested now. I'm ready for the week.

122
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:47,300
That's great. I feel tired but happy.

123
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:50,020
So we had two very different weekends.

124
00:07:50,020 --> 00:07:52,260
Yes, but both were good.

125
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:58,420
Exactly. A weekend can be busy and fun or quiet and relaxing. Both are good.

126
00:07:58,420 --> 00:08:00,180
That's a very good point, Jack.

127
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:01,140
Thank you, Emma.

128
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:06,500
So let's think about the words we use. How do we ask about the weekend?

129
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:09,380
The simple question is, how was your weekend?

130
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:16,820
And we can answer, it was good, it was great, it was busy, it was relaxing, it was quiet.

131
00:08:16,820 --> 00:08:20,260
And we can say, it was terrible if it was a bad weekend.

132
00:08:21,860 --> 00:08:25,140
Let's hope not. We can also ask more questions.

133
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:30,260
Yes, like, what did you do on Saturday? Or what did you do on Sunday?

134
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:37,220
And we can ask about specific things. Did you go out? Did you see any friends? Did you watch any

135
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:43,060
movies. Did you eat at any restaurants? That's my favorite question. Of course it is. Let's

136
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:49,860
practice a little more. Let's talk about the past tense. Ah yes. When we talk about the weekend,

137
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:58,260
we use the past tense. For example, I went, not I go. Right. I saw a movie. I met my friend.

138
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:06,020
I ate pizza. I read a book. I watched TV. I cleaned my kitchen. I slept a lot. You really did.

139
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:09,940
So it's important to remember these past tense verbs.

140
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:14,740
But don't worry if it's difficult. Just practice. You can say simple sentences.

141
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:18,340
Yes. I went to the park is a perfect sentence.

142
00:09:18,340 --> 00:09:22,260
Let's imagine another weekend. A hypothetical weekend.

143
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:25,220
Hypothetical? That's a big word, Jack.

144
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:31,140
I mean, let's imagine a different weekend. Let's talk about a weekend in the summer.

145
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:36,820
Okay. So, Jack, what did you do last summer weekend? Let's imagine.

146
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:41,220
Last summer weekend, I went to the beach.

147
00:09:41,220 --> 00:09:43,540
Oh, wonderful. How was the weather?

148
00:09:43,540 --> 00:09:46,900
It was hot and sunny. Perfect beach weather.

149
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,820
What did you do at the beach?

150
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:53,700
I swam in the sea. The water was a little cold, but it was nice.

151
00:09:53,700 --> 00:09:55,300
Did you build a sand castle?

152
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:59,620
No, I didn't build a sand castle, but I walked on the sand.

153
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,640
I listened to the waves. It was very peaceful.

154
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:04,320
Did you get a sunburn?

155
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:08,080
Oh, yes. I forgot the sunscreen. My shoulders were red.

156
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:10,800
Oh, no. That's not good. You need to be careful.

157
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:13,440
I know. Next time, I will use sunscreen.

158
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:17,520
What about you, Emma? What did you do last summer weekend?

159
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,640
Last summer weekend, I went camping with my friends.

160
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:22,560
Camping? In a tent?

161
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:26,000
Yes, in a tent. We went to the mountains.

162
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:26,880
Was it fun?

163
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:30,320
It was very fun. We put up our tents near a lake.

164
00:10:30,320 --> 00:10:33,360
That sounds beautiful. What did you do there?

165
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:39,600
We went hiking. We walked in the forest. We saw many beautiful trees and flowers.

166
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:41,040
Did you cook food?

167
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:46,400
Yes, we cooked food on a campfire. We made soup and we grilled fish.

168
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:49,040
Grilled fish? Where did you get the fish?

169
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:51,600
From the lake, we went fishing in the morning.

170
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:54,320
You went fishing? I didn't know you liked fishing.

171
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:57,520
I love fishing. It is very relaxing.

172
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:59,520
Wow. Did you catch many fish?

173
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:02,800
I caught two fish. They were small, but delicious.

174
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:06,640
That is so cool. And at night, was it scary in the tent?

175
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:13,440
No, it wasn't scary. It was amazing. We looked at the stars. There were no city lights,

176
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:16,960
so we saw thousands of stars.

177
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:20,960
That sounds incredible. Maybe I should try camping one day.

178
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:24,320
You should, but remember the sunscreen.

179
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:32,320
Yes, I will. So weekends can be for going to new places like the beach or the mountains.

180
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:37,840
Yes, they can. But sometimes a weekend at home is also perfect.

181
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:41,600
I agree. The important thing is to rest and do things you enjoy.

182
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:42,640
Exactly.

183
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:47,040
Let's imagine a winter weekend now. It's cold and rainy outside.

184
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:52,480
Okay. So, Jack, what did you do last winter weekend?

185
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:57,760
Last winter weekend, the weather was terrible. It was cold and rainy.

186
00:11:57,760 --> 00:12:00,560
So what did you do? Did you stay at home?

187
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:04,400
Yes, I stayed at home all weekend, and it was wonderful.

188
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:07,840
What did you do at home?

189
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:12,800
I made hot chocolate. I wore warm, comfortable clothes.

190
00:12:12,800 --> 00:12:13,840
Sounds cozy.

191
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:19,200
It was. I watched many movies. I watched a trilogy of fantasy movies.

192
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:20,880
All three in one weekend?

193
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,480
Yes, it was a movie marathon.

194
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:25,520
A movie marathon? I like that idea.

195
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:30,320
I also played video games for a few hours and I finished my mystery book.

196
00:12:30,320 --> 00:12:33,120
So you had a very indoor weekend.

197
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:36,640
Yes, and I loved it. Sometimes you need a weekend like that.

198
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:41,600
I agree. My perfect winter weekend is similar. I like to bake.

199
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,680
Oh, you bake. What do you bake?

200
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:48,800
I bake cookies or cakes. Last winter, I baked a big apple cake.

201
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:52,240
Apple cake, my favorite. Can I have some?

202
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:59,760
Maybe next time. So, I bake, I drink tea, and I call my friends on the phone.

203
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:04,400
That sounds lovely. So, our weekends can change with the seasons.

204
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:09,120
Yes, they can. The activities can be different. But the feeling is the same.

205
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:12,320
A weekend is for you, for your free time.

206
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:13,360
Well said, Jack.

207
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:18,320
Okay, Jack. We talked a lot about our weekends.

208
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:21,360
I think this is a good time to look at some useful words we used.

209
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:24,320
A vocabulary review. Excellent idea.

210
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:27,040
Let's help our friends remember some key words.

211
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:29,600
Let's start with a word we both used a lot.

212
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:31,600
The first word is relaxing.

213
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:37,680
Relaxing. R-E-L-A-X-I-N-G.

214
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:46,320
G. It's an adjective. It means calm, peaceful, not stressful. It makes you feel restful.

215
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:52,840
Can you use it in a sentence, Jack? Of course. My weekend was very relaxing. It means I felt

216
00:13:52,840 --> 00:14:01,540
calm and happy. I was not nervous. Perfect. Another example. I listen to relaxing music.

217
00:14:01,540 --> 00:14:07,320
It means the music helps you feel calm. What is the opposite of relaxing, Emma?

218
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:13,600
opposite could be stressful. For example, my work is sometimes stressful, but for a

219
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:23,720
weekend we often say busy. Ah yes, busy. B-U-S-Y. My weekend was busy. It means I

220
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:30,480
had many things to do. I had many activities. Exactly. My Saturday was very

221
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:37,160
busy. I went to the cafe, I went shopping, I went to the park, many things. So a

222
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:41,000
A weekend can be relaxing, or it can be busy,

223
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,200
and both can be good.

224
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,120
Yes.

225
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:47,720
Now, let's talk about a word you love, Jack, delicious.

226
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:51,480
I do love this word, delicious.

227
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:56,320
D-E-L-I-C-I-O-U-S.

228
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:59,240
It means very, very good taste.

229
00:14:59,240 --> 00:15:00,080
We use it for,

230
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:05,000
So you don't say the movie was delicious, right?

231
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:12,000
No, that would be funny. This movie is delicious. No. We say a movie is good, funny, or exciting.

232
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:15,000
But food, we say delicious.

233
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,000
So tell me about something delicious from your weekend.

234
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:24,000
The green curry I ordered was delicious. My mom's roast chicken was delicious.

235
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:30,480
And my pizza was delicious. My coffee was delicious. It's a very useful word.

236
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:35,760
It is. Okay, next word. We talked about a special meal. Brunch.

237
00:15:35,760 --> 00:15:42,720
Brunch. B-R-U-N-C-H. This is a combination of breakfast and lunch.

238
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:44,640
When do we eat brunch?

239
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:51,120
We eat brunch late in the morning, maybe between 10 a.m. and 12 p.m.

240
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:56,200
It's for when you wake up late and you are hungry for breakfast, but it's almost lunchtime.

241
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:58,960
So what kind of food is brunch food?

242
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,160
Good question.

243
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:06,600
It can be breakfast food, like eggs, toast, and pancakes, or it can be lunch food, like

244
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:08,320
sandwiches or salads.

245
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:10,120
Often, it's a mix.

246
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:15,600
My sentence is, on Saturday, I woke up late and made brunch.

247
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,640
Perfect.

248
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:20,560
Our next word is a fun activity, movie marathon.

249
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:31,680
Mm-hmm. I love a good movie marathon. Marathon. M-A-R-A-T-H-O-N. Originally, a marathon is

250
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:33,880
a very long running race.

251
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:41,120
Right. So a movie marathon means watching movies for a very long time, one after another.

252
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:47,080
Yes. Like watching all the Superman movies or all the Harry Potter movies in one weekend.

253
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:52,800
a trilogy like you did, Jack. So you don't just watch one movie, you watch a series of

254
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:57,000
movies. Exactly. You can also have a TV show marathon

255
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:03,320
where you watch many episodes of one show. Sometimes we call this binge watching.

256
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:08,040
Binge watching is a more modern word, but movie marathon is very common and easy to

257
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:12,440
understand. Let's do one more word. How about the word

258
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:22,320
rested. Oh, that's a good one. Rested. R-E-S-T-E-D. It is an adjective. It describes how you feel

259
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:28,880
after you rest or sleep. So, if you sleep well, you wake up and feel rested. You have

260
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:36,920
energy. Yes. The opposite is tired, like me today. I am a little tired. I am not feeling

261
00:17:36,920 --> 00:17:43,240
very rested. But I feel very rested because my weekend was quiet and relaxing.

262
00:17:43,240 --> 00:17:50,880
So the verb is to rest and the adjective is rested. I need to rest means I need to relax

263
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:58,200
or sleep. I feel rested means I feel good and energetic because I rested.

264
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:03,760
Great explanation. So let's quickly practice. I will say a sentence and you tell me which

265
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,360
word fits. Okay, I'm ready.

266
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:11,160
Number one, I watched three Star Wars movies on Sunday.

267
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:13,320
It was a fun...

268
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:14,320
That's easy.

269
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:16,720
It was a fun movie marathon.

270
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,820
Correct.

271
00:18:17,820 --> 00:18:21,520
Number two, this soup has a very good taste.

272
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:22,960
It is...

273
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:24,560
It is delicious.

274
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:26,320
Yes.

275
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:28,640
Number three, I didn't do much.

276
00:18:28,640 --> 00:18:31,360
I just read a book and slept.

277
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:33,440
My weekend was very...

278
00:18:33,440 --> 00:18:35,720
It was very relaxing.

279
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:42,680
the last one. I woke up at 11 and made eggs and pancakes. I ate a big…

280
00:18:42,680 --> 00:18:47,440
You ate a big brunch. Excellent. You know all the words, Emma.

281
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:52,560
I hope our friends know them too. Let's repeat the words one more time together.

282
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:56,560
Okay, everyone, repeat after us.

283
00:18:56,560 --> 00:19:16,370
Relaxing, busy, delicious, brunch, movie marathon, rested.

284
00:19:16,370 --> 00:19:17,570
Wonderful.

285
00:19:17,570 --> 00:19:21,870
Try to use one of these words when you answer our question today.

286
00:19:21,870 --> 00:19:26,970
Okay, so today we practice talking about our weekends.

287
00:19:26,970 --> 00:19:31,610
We use the past tense and learn some great new vocabulary words.

288
00:19:31,610 --> 00:19:33,930
And now we have a question for you.

289
00:19:34,570 --> 00:19:36,170
Our question of the day is…

290
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:39,210
What did you do last weekend?

291
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:43,450
Tell us about one thing and try to use one of our new words.

292
00:19:43,450 --> 00:19:49,370
Relaxing, busy, delicious, brunch, movie marathon, or rested?

293
00:19:50,010 --> 00:19:50,730
Yes!

294
00:19:50,730 --> 00:19:53,450
Please write your answer in the comments below.

295
00:19:53,450 --> 00:19:57,570
We read every single one, and we love to learn about your lives.

296
00:19:57,570 --> 00:19:59,530
It is the best part of our week.

297
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:03,840
Thank you so much for watching and for practicing with us today.

298
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:06,240
You are all amazing students.

299
00:20:06,240 --> 00:20:07,240
Keep learning.

300
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:08,640
Keep practicing.

301
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:11,240
See you next time on Daily English Talk.

302
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:11,760
Bye-bye.
